  "rottay": {
    "verdict": "REFUSED BY THE GUARD, not by the writer",
    "measured": "The DB arm emits ZERO variables for every palette-seed write that compiles (measured directly: #DC2626, #4F46E5, #3A6FB0 all -> 0 vars; #22C55E and #A0A0A5 throw on APCA). The same door emits 1 var for density=compact and 1 for typography.scale=0.94, so the DB door works on rottay generally: the inertia is palette-specific.",
    "harnessOutcome": "lowerStop refuses: \"db-tenant-theme lowered primary/crimson through appearance.general.palette.primary and emitted none of the declared channels. That is the finding; it is not an arm.\"",
    "correction": "This REFUTES the design-stage prediction that rottay would be a DESIGNED_NULL with both arms equally inert. The static arm moves 12 channels on rottay while the DB arm emits none: the arms are not equally inert, they diverge."
